From d7c4c8bb356cd09fba058704c60dcf6e1fad1b57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:38:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Corvid v1.5: fixed name, logo leads home, send address,
 share, accessibility

The application is always called Corvid; the name setting is gone (the
support text stays). The mark and name in the header lead to the main
screen. The main screen copies the address the encoder sends the source to,
and "Share" gives every viewer a code of their own for the player, HLS,
RTMP and SRT, with an optional protection of the player. Copying falls back
to a text field when the browser's clipboard refuses. Icon buttons and text
boxes have accessible names, the selected toggle has enough contrast, the
dialog theme is fixed. The status page shows the SRT section only for a
source on the own SRT server. Help explains where the backup stream address
comes from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhjysExATCKDyVfUWLA89B
